1. Area (square feet). The maximum square footage of any sign shall be:
a) Six square feet in the RD, R-45, and R-66 zoning districts;
b) Thirty-two square feet in the GC and GI zoning districts; and
c) In addition to the preceding zoning district regulations, only one building sign may be permitted, and the maximum area of a building sign shall be ten percent, of the total area of the wall (including window and door areas) of which such sign is a part or to which each such sign is most nearly parallel; provided, however, that in no instance shall the building sign exceed 50 square feet;
d) In addition to the preceding zoning district regulations, the maximum area of a directory sign shall be six square feet.
2. Height. The maximum height of any sign shall be:
a) Three feet in the RD, R-45, and R-66 zoning districts;
b) Six feet in the GC and GI zoning districts;
c) When measuring the height of a sign, said measurement shall be to the top of the sign from the higher of the edge-of-pavement elevation at the nearest public street or the normal ground elevation. As used herein, "normal ground elevation" is the elevation along a surface rising at a constant slope form the edge-of-pavement to a point on the building setback having an elevation no higher than the ground floor of the building served by the sign, but it may not be higher than actual ground elevation.
3. Setback. Each sign must have the following setbacks from any right-of-way:
a) Ten feet in the RD, R-45, R-66, GC, and GI zoning districts;
b) In addition to the foregoing setback requirements, signs shall be located such that there is at every street intersection a clear view between heights of three feet and ten square feet in a triangle formed by the corner and points on the curb 30 square feet from the intersection or entranceway.
(Ord. No. 2001-07, § 13.18, 4-10-2001)
